%U A396103 42,69,67,37,62,60,58,55,57,88,56,87,85,49,51,48,50,79,77,75,43,70
%N A396103 Squares visited by a "Spider" (Fers + Alfil + Dabbaba + Knight) moving on a spirally numbered board always to the lowest available unvisited square.
%C A396103 Board is numbered with the square spiral, with initial square labeled 1:
%C A396103 .
%C A396103   17--16--15--14--13
%C A396103    |               |
%C A396103   18   5---4---3  12
%C A396103    |   |       |   |
%C A396103   19   6   1---2  11
%C A396103    |   |           |
%C A396103   20   7---8---9--10
%C A396103    |
%C A396103   21--22--23--24--25
%H A396103 Musketeer Chess, <a href="https://musketeerchess.net/p/games/musketeer/rules/rules-short.php#spider:~:text=buy%20a%20kit-,Spider,-A%20map%20of">Spider</a>
%H A396103 Stephen Emmerson and Geoff Foster, <a href="https://www.theproblemist.org/dloads/Glossary.pdf">A glossary of fairy chess definitions</a>, British Chess Problem Society, 2018.
%H A396103 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fairy_chess_pieces">List of fairy chess pieces</a>
%e A396103 At step 2 square 3 is visited after which square 5 is the lowest available unvisited square, so a(3) = 5.
%Y A396103 Cf. A398717, A316667, A398779, A316884.
